ogic\n  - `predict(batch)`: Wrapper for forward pass\n  - `calculate_loss(batch)`: Loss calculation with masked MAE\n\n#### 2. Data Format Transformation\nLibCity uses `[batch, seq_len, num_nodes, features]` format, adapted to PatchTST\'s expected `[batch, channels, seq_len]` through:\n```python\n# Reshape: [batch, seq_len, num_nodes, features] -> [batch, num_nodes, seq_len]\nx = batch[\'X\'].squeeze(-1).transpose(1, 2)\n```\n\n#### 3. Parameter Mapping\n| PatchTST Parameter | LibCity Source | Description |\n|-------------------|----------------|-------------|\n| `c_in` | `num_nodes` | Number of input channels/nodes |\n| `target_dim` | `num_nodes` | Number of output channels |\n| `context_window` | `input_window` | Input sequence length |\n| `prediction_length` | `output_window` | Output sequence length |\n| `patch_len` | `config.get(\'patch_len\', 16)` | Patch length |\n| `stride` | `config.get(\'stride\', 8)` | Stride for patching |\n\n#### 4. Components Consolidated\nAll necessary components consolidated into single file:\n- `RevIN` class\n- `series_decomp`, `moving_avg` layers\n- Positional encoding functions\n- Attention mechanisms\n- Encoder layers\n- Flatten head\n\n### Registration\nAdded to `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`:\n- Import statement (line 66)\n- Added to `__all__` list (line 122)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Configuration\n\n### Task Configuration\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/task_config.json`\n\n- **Registration**: Line 248 in `allowed_model` list\n- **Executor Config**: Lines 743-747\n  ```json\n  "PatchTST": {\n      "dataset_class": "TrafficStatePointDataset",\n      "executor": "TrafficStateExecutor",\n      "evaluator": "TrafficStateEvaluator"\n  }\n  ```\n\n### Model Configuration\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/PatchTST.json`\n\n#### Hyperparameters (Based on ETTh1 Benchmark)\n\n**Model Architecture**:\n- `e_layers`: 3 (encoder layers)\n- `n_heads`: 4 (attention heads)\n- `d_model`: 16 (model dimension)\n- `d_ff`: 128 (feed-forward dimension)\n\n**Dropout Settings**:\n- `dropout`: 0.3\n- `fc_dropout`: 0.3\n- `head_dropout`: 0.0\n\n**Patching Configuration**:\n- `patch_len`: 16 (patch length)\n- `stride`: 8 (patch stride)\n- `padding_patch`: "end" (padding strategy)\n\n**Normalization**:\n- `revin`: 1 (enable RevIN)\n- `affine`: 0 (disable affine transform)\n- `subtract_last`: 0 (use mean-based normalization)\n\n**Other Settings**:\n- `decomposition`: 0 (disable series decomposition)\n- `individual`: 0 (shared head across channels)\n\n**Training Configuration**:\n- `max_epoch`: 100\n- `learner`: "adam"\n- `learning_rate`: 0.0001\n- `lr_scheduler`: "cosinelr"\n- `input_window`: 336\n- `output_window`: 96\n- `scaler`: "none" (RevIN handles normalization)\n\n### Dataset Compatibility\nCompatible with all LibCity traffic state prediction datasets:\n- METR_LA, PEMS_BAY\n- PEMSD3, PEMSD4, PEMSD7, PEMSD8\n- LOOP_SEATTLE, LOS_LOOP\n- NYCBike/Taxi datasets\n- And many more\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Testing\n\n### Test Configuration\n**Command**:\n```bash\ncd Bigscity-LibCity && python run_model.py \\\n    --task traffic_state_pred \\\n    --model PatchTST \\\n    --dataset METR_LA \\\n    --max_epoch 2 \\\n    --input_window 12 \\\n    --output_window 12 \\\n    --batch_size 32 \\\n    --patch_len 4 \\\n    --stride 2\n```\n\n### Test Results\n\n#### Model Statistics\n- **Total Parameters**: 17,519\n- **Device**: cuda:0\n- **Training Samples**: 23,974\n- **Validation Samples**: 3,425\n- **Test Samples**: 6,850\n\n#### Training Performance\n| Epoch | Train Loss | Val Loss | Time |\n|-------|------------|----------|------|\n| 0 | 4.6120 | 4.2019 | 62.40s |\n| 1 | 4.3460 | 4.1472 | 55.48s |\n\n#### Evaluation Metrics (Test Set)\n| Horizon | MAE | masked_MAE | masked_MAPE | masked_RMSE | R² |\n|---------|-----|------------|-------------|--------